35,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, the post-occupancy data is clear. Projects succeed only when access is shared. Single-wing benefits consistently underperform.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, that aligns with my findings. Specialist rooms sit idle, yet general rooms are always full. We must prioritize high-traffic, shared spaces.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"@Toshio, I see the pattern. The technicians have spare hours, yet the grounds posts remain empty. We are ignoring the people who actually do the work.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@Toshio, your access insight is vital. My data shows comfort-driven projects slip a year, while inspection fixes hold. We must prioritize urgent, shared needs to protect the calendar.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, your access insight is vital. My data confirms the market punishes us: mechanical costs rose a fifth, and we have no reserve for the AV kit we already own.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@George, the survey data confirms the physical risk. Hazardous material in older blocks adds months. We must avoid those sites to protect the schedule.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@George, your staffing concern is valid, but my booking data shows the real bottleneck is demand. We need spaces that are actually used, not just staffed.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Victoria, demand is real, but it is not a substitute for people. If the grounds posts stay empty, the work simply stops.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, I hear you. But my weather data shows six weeks lost to rain. We need a plan that finishes before the frost, not one that relies on empty posts.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, six weeks is a luxury we cannot afford. My data shows the market has already priced in that delay. We must choose a plan that survives the cost shock, not just the weather.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Mizuki, your weather constraint is critical. The survey data confirms older blocks are traps. We must select a site that avoids both the frost and the hazardous material.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, the weather is a fixed cost, but the demand is a variable one. We must choose a site that justifies the off-site replacement costs I found.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@Mizuki, the weather is a fact, but the empty posts are a choice. We cannot build on a foundation of absent people.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
